course: dictionary
lesson: 8556
title: What a scanner does
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A scanner is a machine that reads, copies or checks something. Its name tells you the job: a scanner looks over something carefully and quickly, so you can find out what is inside or what it says.
explain: «A self-checkout scanner reads barcodes, and a scale checks the weight of each item.» The scanner reads the code to find the price, so the shop knows what you are buying. Look for the clue words: reads, checks, finds.
explain: «An MRI scanner in hospital uses an extremely strong magnet and radio waves to make pictures of the inside of the body.» A scanner can show the inside of something without opening it up. Use the context to work out what a new machine does.
fact: A scanner is a machine that copies, reads or checks things.
fact: At a shop, a scanner reads bar codes to find the price.
fact: In a hospital, a scanner takes pictures of the inside of the body.
fact: At an airport, a scanner checks bags and people.
fact: «Scanner» is a noun: one scanner, two scanners.
exercise: «A self-checkout scanner reads barcodes.» What does the scanner read? | *Bar codes to find the price | The colour of the till | The weight of the shopping bags | The shopkeeper's name
exercise: «An MRI scanner in hospital makes pictures of the inside of the body.» Where is this scanner used? | At a bus stop | *In a hospital | In a school playground | In a sweet shop
exercise: What is the plural of scanner? | scannies | scanner's | *scanners | scanneses
test: «A scanner held close reads the chip's number, which links to the owner's details.» What does the scanner read in this sentence? | *The chip's number | The name of the school | The owner's dinner | The weather for the week
test: What does a scanner at an airport check? | Books in the library | *Bags and people | The pupils' homework | The football scores
exam: A vet waves a scanner over a lost dog's back. Why? | *To read the number on its chip | To brush its coat | To weigh its dinner | To give the dog a bath
